  "notes": {
    "raw": "\\*Data except enthalpy of formation at 298 K estimated. \nPhase changes: 903.9 K, melting point of Sb; $\\Delta H^{\\circ} = 4.750$ kcal/mol. \n1860 K, boiling point of Sb to equilibrium mixture of $Sb(g)$ , $Sb_{2}(g)$ , and $Sb_{4}(g)$ . \nHeat capacity (cal/mol·K) and enthalpy (kcal/mol) equations: \n298.15-3000 K: $Cp^{0} = 31.676 + 0.056 \\times 10^{-3} T - 2.102 \\times 10^{5} T^{-2}$ \n$H^{\\circ}-H_{298}^{\\circ}=31.676\\times10^{-3}T+0.028\\times10^{-6}T^{2}+2.102\\times10^{2}T^{-1}-10.152$ \nReaction equations (kcal/mol): \n298.15-903.9 K: $\\Delta \\mathrm{Hr}^{\\circ} = -40.584 + 4.814 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} - 2.956 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 116.800 \\mathrm{T}^{-1}$ \n$\\Delta Gr^{\\circ} = -40.584 - 4.814 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} \\ln \\mathrm{T} + 2.956 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 58.400 \\mathrm{T}^{-1} + 58.627 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T}$ \n903.9-1860 K: $\\Delta Hr^{\\circ} = -47.591 - 0.010 \\times 10^{-3} T - 0.612 \\times 10^{-6} T^{2} + 73.600 T^{-1}$ \n$\\Delta Gr^{\\circ} = -47.591 + 0.010 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} \\ln \\mathrm{T} + 0.612 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 36.800 \\mathrm{T}^{-1} + 35.688 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T}$ \nSource: Data based on Prusaczyk (101) who estimated molecular constants. ",
